Subject: Flat Monte Carlo: a counted search that never reads the clock (mtgsim --mc fixed)
Why: Forge's Flat Monte Carlo decides how much to sample by the clock (decision and turn budgets,
  deadlines between rollouts, a cut to the lines the first rollout's time can pay for, a 2 s AI
  timeout inside copies, a pause after slow decisions), so a seeded game with --mc on|max does
  not replay. Adds AiController.setFlatMonteCarloCountOnly: for that player the search size is
  fixed in lines and rounds (Config.counted), the turn budget is 100 rollouts instead of
  seconds, and none of those clock checks run. The counted turn budget is needed: without it a
  play that cannot be put on the stack was chosen again and again until the game timed out
  (3 of 40 games).
Measured: Forge 7db198d72e with patches 0001-0008, Azorius Control vs Boros Dwarves (meta lists).
  Without Monte Carlo the patch changes nothing: `mtgsim match ... -n 200 --seed 1` gave 200 of
  200 identical games without and with it. `-n 40 --seed 7 --mc fixed`: 40 of 40 games identical
  with 1 and 2 workers and on a second run, no timeouts (before the turn budget: 3 of 40). Mirror
  (Boros Dwarves, 100 games, seed 5): 50.0% (40-60). Azorius Control piloted `fixed` against the
  default AI, 200 games, seed 1: 32.0% (26-39) against 26.0% (20-32) with the default pilot,
  +6.0 points (95% interval -2.9 to +14.8): not a reliable gain. 0.08-0.14 s per rollout, 178
  rollouts and 21 s per game for one searching seat (2.3 s without). See VALIDATION.md.
  Revised 17 Nov 2026: AiController.setFlatMonteCarloCountedDepth and Config.counted(depth) size the
  counted search by a depth (1 = the search above; mtgsim --mc deep plays depth 8: up to 8 approved
  and 5 discovered lines, 2 target variants, 32 rounds plus 16, 800 rollouts a turn). Depth 1 is
  unchanged: Azorius Control vs Boros Dwarves, `-n 12 --seed 7 --mc fixed`, 12 of 12 games
  identical before and after. Depth 8 replays: `-n 4 --seed 7 --mc deep` with 2 and 4 workers gave
  identical games and rollout counts. Cost with both seats searching: 6.6 rollouts a decision and
  54 s a game at depth 1, 14.2 and 105 s at depth 4, 23.6 and 186 s at depth 8 (pruning keeps the
  real growth below the nominal one). Strength: Dimir Uldaros's seat against the default-piloted
  meta, 540 games per arm, seed 1: fixed 45.2% (41-49), deep 44.4% (40-49), deep - fixed -0.7
  (paired -3.6 to +2.1) at 2.9 times the rollouts. No gain; see VALIDATION.md, "The pilot" (iv).

